## Safety and architecture invariants

- Use strict TDD: observe RED before production code, then minimal GREEN, then refactor.
- Keep commits small and coherent; commit at each verified feature increment.
- Migrations must be additive, idempotent, rollback-safe, and preserve unknown history as NULL/UNKNOWN.
- Never destructively rewrite existing live state to make tests pass.
- Claims must use `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, durable ownership, monotonically increasing fencing tokens, and partial unique indexes.
- PID identity must include boot ID, `/proc/<pid>/stat` start ticks, executable, working directory, and cgroup/systemd-unit identity. PID alone is not authority.
- Durable exit receipts must prevent invented exit codes. Missing receipt means UNKNOWN/RECOVERY_NEEDED, not fabricated failure or success.
- Lease expiry must fence and reconcile the exact old process tree before releasing conflict capacity.
- Separate lease/liveness, useful-progress deadline, and absolute deadline.
- Workers must be isolated with per-attempt worktrees and an OS write boundary. Canonical repo, DB, gate, evidence, credentials, and user units must be read-only/inaccessible from the worker.
- Worker route policy must fail closed for direct, inherited, auxiliary, and pool fallbacks. Persist requested route, actual hops, request IDs, and billing classification. Unknown cost is `UNKNOWN`, never `FREE`.
- Structured handoff must include identities, base/candidate SHA range, files, requirements, commands/results, hashes, blockers, and route data. Reject stale, malformed, escaped, contradictory, altered, or out-of-scope handoffs.
- Independent verification must run verifier-owned commands against the candidate before integration.
- Integration must be serialized, check clean/unchanged canonical state, handle full commit ranges, record candidate-to-canonical mapping, and recover idempotently from post-Git/pre-DB crashes.
- Repeated equivalent failures must produce one bounded diagnosis/split/replan task, not an infinite retry loop.
- An incomplete empty queue, missing dependency, or cycle must become durable diagnosis/blocker state.
- The final gate is keyed by exact repo SHA, spec hash, and verifier policy revision. Any code/spec/policy change invalidates prior acceptance.
- Native AR/device evidence remains incomplete until actually observed on the required environment.
- Never signal a historical PID without revalidating start ticks, executable, cwd, and ownership immediately before the signal.

